> "realities" (I think monolinguals with little to no foreign language
> experience in particular are very good at deluding themselves into thinki=
ng
> that the way their language implicitly substitutes certain letters/symbol=
s
> with non-correspondant phonemes is natural and possibly even inate to all
> human speech), and instruct the reader that it is definitely not correct =
in
